<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.1 </span>More ablation study on OpenSora.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To demonstrate the adaptability and generalization ability of our method across different tasks, we not only report additional main experimental results, but also include ablation studies conducted on OpenSora.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Tab. <a href="#A2.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ B.3 More Ablation Study ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ SODA: Sensitivity-Oriented Dynamic Acceleration for Diffusion Transformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, compared to the vanilla caching strategy, our proposed DCS module improves performance by 1.96% on average by minimizing cumulative caching error through dynamic programming based on estimated error. In addition, the adaptive pruning mechanism (UAS) corrects caching error by retaining important tokens, resulting in a 2% improvement. The combination of both modules leads to an average increase of 2.08 on the VBench, with nearly a 4% gain in imaging quality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">On the one hand, this demonstrates the effectiveness of our proposed modules; on the other hand, it highlights the general applicability of our SODA.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07057v1/visual_dit.png" id="A2.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:672/479;" width="672" height="479" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F12.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A2.F12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization results of different acceleration methods on DiT-XL/2.<span id="A2.F12.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Comparisons are highlighted with red dashed boxes.
</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F13" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2603.07057v1/visual_pixart.png" id="A2.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:665/608;" width="665" height="608" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F13.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="A2.F13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Visualization results of different acceleration methods on PixArt-<math id="A2.F13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.F13.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">.
</span></span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.2 </span>More parameter analysis on PixArt.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To further demonstrate the robustness of the hyperparameters introduced by the UAS module, in addition to the parameter space reported on DiT in the main text, we also report results on the parameter space explored on PixArt in Tab. <a href="#A2.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ B.3 More Ablation Study ‣ Appendix B More Experiments ‣ SODA: Sensitivity-Oriented Dynamic Acceleration for Diffusion Transformer" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It can be observed that the FID fluctuates within a narrow range of 0.14 across the entire parameter space, indicating a high degree of robustness and suggesting that our method is largely insensitive to the hyperparameters introduced in UAS.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Typically, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed. Given acceleration factor <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we first obtain the number of cache interval <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{s}=N/r-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{s}=N/r-1</annotation></semantics></math> (leave room for pruning), then select <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>: <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}^{T}\sum_{l}^{L}\{\lambda\mathcal{E}_{c}(t,l,n)+\beta\}=1/r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>l</mi><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}^{T}\sum_{l}^{L}\{\lambda\mathcal{E}_{c}(t,l,n)+\beta\}=1/r</annotation></semantics></math> (omit transformation from <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>), it means the proportion of pruned tokens is the inverse of speed-up factor. Due to the adaptive pruning decisions, <math id="A2.SS3.SSS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> may fluctuate slightly, but it has negligible impact on acceleration factor.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T13" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A2.T13.3" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:233.5pt;height:39.4pt;vertical-align:-18.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-64.3pt,10.9pt) scale(0.644794614456059,0.644794614456059) ;">
<table id="A2.T13.3.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A2.T13.3.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T13.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.5pt 4.0pt;">DiT-XL/2</td>
<td id="A2.T13.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.5pt 4.0pt;">FlashAtt</td>
<td id="A2.T13.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.5pt 4.0pt;">Lat.(s)↓</td>
<td id="A2.T13.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.5pt 4.0pt;">Spe.↑</td>
<td id="A2.T13.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.5pt 4.0pt;">IS↑</td>
<td id="A2.T13.3.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.5pt 4.0pt;">FID↓</td>
